hadiths[20]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27938","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah, he said: Abd Allah ibn Utbah ibn Abi Sufyan informed me: My paternal aunt Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he was with her on her day or her night, and he heard the caller to prayer, he said as the caller to prayer says."
"27939","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from al-Numan ibn Salim, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, he said: Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: Whoever prays in a day twelve rakahs, voluntary other than obligatory, a house shall be built for him in Paradise."
"27940","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, he said: I heard Salim ibn Shawwal saying, from Umm Habibah, she said: We used to depart early in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from Jam to Mina. And Samurah said: We used to depart early in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from al-Muzdalifah to Mina."
"27941","Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Salim, from Abu al-Jarrah, from Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"27942","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Humayd ibn Nafi narrated to me, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, that Umm Habibah, a relative or kinsman of hers died, so she called for yellow perfume and wiped her forearms with it, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is not lawful for a woman believing in Allah and the Last Day to mourn a dead person over three days, except for a husband, for she mourns him four months and ten days."
"27943","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Sufyan ibn Said, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"27944","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi informed me, from Salim, from Abu al-Jarrah, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"27945","Abu Bakr ibn Khallad narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Said, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"27946","He said: I said to him: May you be wretched, O Abu Abd Allah. He said to me: How is it. I said: Ubayd Allah narrated to me, he said: Nafi narrated to me, from Salim, from Abu al-Jarrah, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: You spoke the truth."
"27947","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Damrah ibn Habib, from Muhammad ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray with a garment over him and over me, and therein was what was."
"27948","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shuaythi narrated to us, and Yazid said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shuaythi informed us, from his father, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from his sister Umm Habibah, Yazid said: bint Abi Sufyan, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and al-Muqri said: the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that she heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever prays four rakahs before noon and four after it, Allah forbids him to the Fire."
"27949","Hajjaj and Shuayb ibn Harb said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that he asked his sister Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray in the single garment in which he was intimate with her. She said: Yes, if there was no filth therein."
"27950","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, and Rawh said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ata informed me that Ibn Shawwal informed him that he entered upon Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, and she informed him that he sent, and Ibn Bakr said: that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent her from Jam at night. And Yahya said: He sent her ahead from Jam at night."
"27951","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Harb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, that Abu Sufyan ibn al-Mughirah al-Thaqafi narrated to him that he entered upon Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she called for sawiq for him, and he drank. She said to him: O son of my brother, will you not perform ablution. He said: I have not innovated impurity. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"27952","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Darraj narrated to us, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, that he narrated to him, from Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, that some people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he taught them prayer, and the practices, and the obligations. Then they said: O Messenger of Allah, we have a drink we make from wheat and barley. He said: Al-Ghubayra. They said: Yes. He said: Do not consume it. Then after that, two days later, they mentioned them to him also, and he said: Al-Ghubayra. They said: Yes. He said: Do not consume it. Then when they intended to depart, they asked him about it, and he said: Al-Ghubayra. They said: Yes. He said: Do not consume it. They said: Then they will not leave it. He said: Whoever does not leave it, strike his neck."
"27953","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, my father said, and Ali ibn Ishaq: Abd Allah informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Umm Habibah, that she was under Ubayd Allah ibn Jahsh, and he came to the Negus, and Ali ibn Ishaq said: And he journeyed to the Negus, and died; and that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married Umm Habibah while she was in the land of Abyssinia; the Negus married her to him, and dowered her four thousand, then prepared her from his own, and sent her to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with Shurahbil ibn Hasanah; and all her trousseau was from the Negus, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not send anything to her; and the dowers of the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were four hundred dirhams."
"27954","Hashim narrated to us: al-Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us: Nafi narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from al-Jarrah, the freedman of Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he heard him informing Abd Allah ibn Umar that Umm Habibah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The caravan in which there is a bell, the angels do not accompany it."
"27955","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us: Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed us, and he mentioned this hadith following the hadiths of Ibn Abi Husayn, and said: I am Anas ibn Malik, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: I saw what my nation shall meet after me, and the shedding of some of them of the blood of others; and that preceded from Allah, Exalted is He, as it preceded in the nations; so I asked Him to grant me intercession on the Day of Resurrection for them, and He did. Abd Allah said: I said to my father: Here are people narrating it from Abu al-Yaman, from Shuayb, from al-Zuhri. He said: This is not from the hadith of al-Zuhri; it is only from the hadith of Ibn Abi Husayn."
"27956","Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever prays in a day twelve rakahs besides the obligatory, Allah, Exalted is He, builds for him, or he said: there shall be built for him a house in Paradise."
"27957","Yaqub narrated to us: Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Zaynab bint Abi Salamah informed him that Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed her that she said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: O Messenger of Allah, marry my sister, the daughter of Abi Sufyan. She claimed that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Do you like that. She said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; I am not exclusive to you, and the dearest to share me in good is my sister. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: That is not lawful to me. I said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we indeed talk that you intend to marry Durrah bint Abi Salamah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The daughter of Umm Salamah. She said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Allah, had she not been my stepdaughter in my care, she would not be lawful to me; she is the daughter of my milk brother, and Thuwaybah nursed me and Abu Salamah; so do not offer to me your daughters nor your sisters."
